hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1469","On the authority of Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Qaisi, on the authority of Abu Mutarrif bin Abi Al-Wazir, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Amr Al-Raqi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “would not go out on the day of Eid until he had eaten food. He went out and prayed two rak'ahs for the people, and when he returned, he prayed two rak'ahs in his house, and he did not pray anything before the prayer.”"
